    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98">

                <pb facs="0239" n="140" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg140"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.00/3577: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-08T20:00:00+01:00">March 8, 1936—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 8—5:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>63. Following Hitler’s speech of yesterday<anchor n="2" xml:id="d98-f1"/>
                    Reichstag President Goering read the following message from Hitler: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“For the purpose of giving the German people the opportunity of being
                            able to bestow their solemn approval on the 3-year policy concluded
                            today of the restoration of the national honor and sovereignty of the
                            Reich joined with upright endeavor for a true reconciliation and
                            understanding of peoples on the basis of like rights and like
                            obligations, I dissolve the Reichstag with the expiration of March 28,
                            1936. New elections to the Reichstag will take place on Sunday, March
                            29, 1936.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Goebbels<anchor n="3" xml:id="d98-f2"/> will open campaign by speech on March 10.
                    It is generally considered that Hitler has been waiting the first available
                    opportunity for a vote reaffirming his position. This affords a perfect
                    occasion.</p>
                <p>Repeated by wire to Paris, London; by air mail to Rome, Geneva, Moscow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodd</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d98-f1" n="2" xml:id="d98-f1-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi>, March 8, 1936, p. 32. For
                    correspondence regarding the Hitler speech of March 7 and the reoccupation of
                    the Rhineland, see <ref target="frus1936v01#pg_180">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, pp. 180</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d98-f2" n="3" xml:id="d98-f2-content">
                <p>Joseph Goebbels, Minister for National Enlightenment and Propaganda.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
